---
description: Best practices for using Tailwind CSS in your project
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx,css}
---
- Use utility-first approach for styling to keep your CSS modular and reusable.
- Organize your Tailwind CSS classes in a logical order (e.g., layout, spacing, typography, colors).
- Utilize Tailwind's responsive utilities to create mobile-friendly designs.
- Keep your Tailwind configuration file clean and well-documented.
- Use Tailwind's `@apply` directive sparingly and only when necessary for complex styles.

